    {
      "section": "6.8",
      "label": "(10)",
      "text": "If the drug volume in the reservoir measures less than Vers =0.5 ml, and an infusion is in progress, an empty-reservoir alarm shall be issued stopping the pump.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "6.9",
      "label": "(1)",
      "text": "The drug library can be thought of as a lookup table that, given a drug name and a location, provides typical and safe limits of diﬀerent infusion parameters.",
